cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, or the mushroom-body compartment correction it
  documents, please cite it using the metadata below. Please also cite the
  FlyEM male CNS connectome dataset separately — it is CC-BY 4.0 and its
  attribution obligation travels with every derived artifact.
title: >-
  FLYFAM: a simulated Drosophila connectome trading Pons v2 memecoins on paper,
  with holder-voted exits
abstract: >-
  A leaky integrate-and-fire simulation of the FlyEM male Drosophila CNS
  connectome v1.0 (165,122 traced neurons, 10,228,000 signed edges), wired to a
  live memecoin market on Robinhood Chain through a pre-registered sensory
  encoder and action decoder. Includes a correction to a transposed
  dopaminergic read in the upstream mushroom-body plasticity code, a
  pre-registered associative-conditioning experiment against the corrected
  compartment split, and a holder-voted paper-trading product. Execution is
  paper only: nothing is signed or broadcast, and no claim of trading skill is
  made.
type: software
authors:
  - name: FLYFAM
    website: 'https://flyfam.xyz'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/maumcrez-svg/flyfam'
url: 'https://flyfam.xyz'
keywords:
  - connectomics
  - Drosophila
  - mushroom body
  - spiking neural network
  - leaky integrate-and-fire
  - associative conditioning
  - paper trading
references:
  - type: data
    title: >-
      FlyEM male Drosophila central nervous system connectome, version 1.0
      (MaleCNS v1.0)
    authors:
      - name: HHMI Janelia FlyEM
      - name: Cambridge Connectomics Group
      - name: Google Research
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: >-
      The dataset is not redistributed in this repository. Source URLs, byte
      sizes and sha256 for the three feather tables are in data/MANIFEST.md.
  - type: software
    title: flycoinrh
    authors:
      - name: fruitflydev
    repository-code: 'https://github.com/fruitflydev/flycoinrh'
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      Vendored unmodified under upstream/ at commit
      5aab4e7895a1f5930319bf3bde8010b350a163a2 and byte-pinned by
      docs/UPSTREAM_MANIFEST.txt. The mushroom-body compartment correction in
      this project is a fix to a defect in that code, made in our own modules;
      no upstream file is modified. A standalone minimal repro and fix is at
      https://github.com/maumcrez-svg/flysim-mushroom-fix
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A leaky integrate-and-fire computational model based on the connectome of
      the entire adult Drosophila brain reveals insights into sensorimotor
      processing
    authors:
      - family-names: Shiu
        given-names: Philip K.
    year: 2024
    notes: The simulation approach this project reuses from upstream follows this work.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Connectome-constrained networks predict neural activity across the fly
      visual system
    authors:
      - family-names: Lappalainen
        given-names: Janne K.
    year: 2024
    notes: Referenced by the upstream simulator's modelling approach.
